+# Story 5.1: Query Language Design
+
+## Business Context
+
+Security analysts need to search events without learning SQL. This story delivers the foundational language design for AxiQL -- the grammar specification (EBNF), AST type hierarchy, Chumsky parser scaffold, field alias registry, multi-version OCSF query semantics, and type system specification. It does not implement the full parser (that is Story 5.2) but establishes all the language artifacts that downstream stories build on.
+
+This is the highest-leverage story in Epic 5: every subsequent query story (5.2 through 5.7) depends on the language design decisions made here. The grammar spec (`axiql-grammar-specification.md`) serves as the single source of truth per SOUL.md #3 -- the Chumsky code implements it, not the other way around.
+
+## Technical Guardrails
+
+- **Parser library:** Chumsky 0.10 (replaces Pest project-wide). Decision rationale: error recovery, `Send + Sync`, context-sensitive parsing.
+- **Grammar documentation:** EBNF notation (ISO 14977) in `axiql-grammar-specification.md`. This is the spec; Chumsky code is the implementation.
+- **Shared types in `axiathon-core`:** `FieldRef`, `Value`, `CompareOp`, `StringOp` live in `axiathon-core` because the Detection DSL (`axiathon-detection`, Story 3.2) also uses them. Do not put these in `axiathon-query`.
+- **AxiQL-only types in `axiathon-query`:** `AxiQLStatement`, `FilterExpr`, `SelectExpr`, `PipeStage`, `AggregationExpr`, `Source`, `OrderByExpr`, etc.
+- **DataFusion dotted-column gotcha:** `col("user.name")` is interpreted as `table.column` by DataFusion. Must use `Column::new(None::<&str>, "user.name")` via a `field_col()` helper. This constraint influences `FieldRef` design.
+- **Three-tier alias resolution:** analyst shortcut -> AxiQL canonical -> OCSF canonical. Resolution at query planning time, after parsing, before LogicalPlan construction.
+- **No `unwrap()` in production code** -- use `?` or `expect()` with actionable message.
+
+### Key Files to Create
+
+| File | Purpose |
+|------|---------|
+| `crates/axiathon-core/src/query_types.rs` | `FieldRef`, `Value`, `CompareOp`, `StringOp` |
+| `crates/axiathon-query/src/ast.rs` | Full AxiQL AST type hierarchy |
+| `crates/axiathon-query/src/parser.rs` | Chumsky parser scaffold with `parse_axiql()` entry point |
+| `crates/axiathon-query/src/aliases.rs` | `FieldAliasRegistry`, three-tier resolution |
+| `crates/axiathon-query/src/version.rs` | `OcsfVersionFilter`, multi-version semantics |
+| `crates/axiathon-query/src/type_system.rs` | `AxiQLType`, `TypeConstraint`, `TypeError` |
+| `docs/reference/query-syntax.md` | User-facing syntax reference with examples |
+
+### Dependencies
+
+| Crate | Version | Usage |
+|-------|---------|-------|
+| `chumsky` | 0.10 | Parser combinator framework |
+| `serde` | 1 | AST serialization |
+| `semver` | 1 | OCSF version parsing |
+| `strsim` | 0.11 | Edit distance for typo suggestions |
+
+## Scope Boundaries
+
+**In scope:**
+- EBNF grammar spec for all three AxiQL modes (filter, SQL, pipe)
+- Shared foundation types in `axiathon-core` (`FieldRef`, `Value`, `CompareOp`, `StringOp`)
+- Complete AST type hierarchy in `axiathon-query`
+- Chumsky parser scaffold (compiles, mode detection wired, entry point exists)
