+
+## AC Context
+
+**AC-1 (Filter mode syntax):** The parser scaffold must wire the filter mode grammar covering: field comparisons (`=`, `!=`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=`), wildcards (`*`, `?`), boolean operators (`AND`/`&&`, `OR`/`||`, `NOT`/`!`), parenthesized grouping, existence (`HAS`, `MISSING`), regex (`=~`), string operators (`CONTAINS`, `STARTSWITH`, `ENDSWITH` + case-insensitive variants), list membership (`IN`, `NOT IN`), CIDR matching. Edge cases: deeply nested parentheses, mixed operator precedence, empty field values.
+
+**AC-2 (SQL mode syntax):** `SELECT` with field refs, `*`, aggregation functions (COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX, DISTINCT_COUNT, PERCENTILE), column aliases, `FROM` with source tables (EVENTS, ALERTS, SESSIONS, ASSETS, custom views), `WHERE`, `GROUP BY`, `ORDER BY` (ASC/DESC), `LIMIT`. Edge cases: SELECT without FROM, multiple aliases, aggregation without GROUP BY.
+
+**AC-3 (Pipe mode syntax):** Filter expression followed by `|`-separated stages: `stats` (with `BY` grouping), `sort` (with direction), `head N`, `tail N`, `dedup`, `fields +/-`. Edge cases: pipe with no stages (just filter), multiple consecutive pipe stages, empty stage.
+
+**AC-4 (OCSF field references):** Dotted paths (`src.ip`, `user.name`), analyst shortcuts (`src_ip` -> `src.ip` -> `src_endpoint.ip`), vendor extensions (`unmapped['claroty.alert_type']`). Three-tier alias resolution must be defined in the alias registry structure.
+
+**AC-5 (Multi-version OCSF):** Default routes to latest version. `ocsf_version:1.7.0` for specific version. `ocsf_version:*` for cross-version union (superset schema, NULL for missing, CAST for type differences). `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.OCSF_EVENT_CLASSES` and `INFORMATION_SCHEMA.OCSF_VERSIONS` metadata tables.
+
+**AC-6 (Chumsky scaffold compiles):** `cargo build -p axiathon-query` succeeds. Mode detection via `choice()` is wired. `parse_axiql(input: &str) -> (Option<AxiQLStatement>, Vec<AxiQLError>)` exists.
+
+**AC-7 (Shared types in axiathon-core):** `FieldRef` (segments + optional array index, Display, FromStr), `Value` (String, Integer, Float, Boolean, Regex, Duration), `CompareOp`, `StringOp`. All with appropriate derives.
+
+**AC-8 (AxiQL AST types):** Complete hierarchy: `AxiQLStatement`, `FilterExpr` (9 variants), `SelectExpr`, `AggregationExpr`, `AggFunction`, `Source`, `PipeStage` (6 variants), `OrderByExpr`, `SortDirection`, `FieldsMode`.
+
+**AC-9 (Error reporting):** `AxiQLError` with span, expected/found, label, hint. Type mismatch errors with actionable hints. Position reporting as line:column.
+
+**AC-10 (Documentation):** `docs/reference/query-syntax.md` covering all three modes, operator precedence, field aliases, multi-version semantics, 10+ example queries for common security use cases.
+
+**AC-11 (Config limits):** Query execution limits (`default_timeout_secs`, `max_timeout_secs`, `max_result_rows`, `max_concurrent_queries`, `max_memory_per_query_mb`) specified as hot-reloadable config values. Depends on Story 1.20 (Configuration Infrastructure).
